[center][color=#00ffff][size=6][b]Sprintware[/b][/size][/color]
[i]Quickhack your own legs.[/i]

[size=2]Made on request for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/profile/TheRealJonCross]TheRealJonCross[/url].[/size][/center]
[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]What This Is[/b][/size][/color]
For a city famous for human enhancement, V runs surprisingly like a normal person. Sprintware is a small CET mod that adds a configurable speed boost you can toggle with a hot key. Think of it as a piece of locomotion firmware your ripperdoc forgot to install.

Bind a key. Press it. Run faster. Press it again. Run normal. That is the entire mod.

[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Features[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][b]Toggle keybind[/b] and a [b]boost slider[/b] (0 to +15 m/s, default +8), both set in Native Settings.
[*][b]Live updates[/b]: change the slider while the boost is on and the new value takes effect immediately.
[*][b]Boost starts off[/b] every time you load a save. Stops you sprinting off a balcony you forgot about.
[*][b]Optional debug overlay[/b]: a small on-screen readout of your current MaxSpeed, velocity, and Reflexes. Off by default, toggle it on in the settings tab.
[/list]
[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]How It Works[/b][/size][/color]
The boost adds a flat bonus to the player's MaxSpeed stat. It only affects how fast V moves on foot. Vehicles, NPCs, time of day, animation speed, all untouched.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]About the Speed Cap[/b][/size][/color]
Cyberpunk 2077 has a hard 15 m/s ceiling on the player's MaxSpeed stat (about 54 km/h). The slider lets you go up to +15 m/s of additive boost, but your total speed (base sprint + Reflexes bonus + this mod's boost) clamps at 15. Once you hit the cap, more slider does nothing.

In practice, +5 to +10 m/s feels great. Higher values still apply, but you may not feel the difference past the cap.

If you have the Reflexes "Mad Dash" perk, you may notice that dashing while the boost is active briefly hits roughly 30 m/s. That is not a feature of this mod. The dash uses a different velocity mechanism that the engine lets temporarily exceed the cap. Happy accident, free of charge.

[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url]
[/list]
[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
Install the requirements, then extract the archive into your Cyberpunk 2077 game directory.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size][/color]
Delete the following folder:
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]bin\x64\plugins\cyber_engine_tweaks\mods\sprintware\[/font]
[/list]
[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Status[/b][/size][/color]
This mod is feature complete. I will fix bugs as they come up. I do not plan to add new features.

[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Pure CET runtime mod. Does not replace, modify, or stream any game files.
[*]No Redscript, no TweakXL, no ArchiveXL. Compatible with anything that does not fight over the player's MaxSpeed stat.
[*]Other mods that boost MaxSpeed will stack additively with this one. The 15 m/s cap still applies to the total.
[/list]
[line]
[color=#00ffff][size=5][b]Disclaimer[/b][/size][/color]
This mod was developed with the assistance of an LLM. All in-game testing and code validation was performed by a human. No rogue AIs were permitted through the Blackwall.
